<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Taputapuatea</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Taputapuatea marae</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Taputapuatea is a marae complex at Opoa on the island of Raiatea in French <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/polynesia">Polynesia</a>, the most important religious centre of eastern Polynesia in the centuries before European contact. Dedicated to the god <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oro">ʻOro</a>, it drew chiefs and priests from across the Society Islands and beyond, and stones from it were used to found other marae. It was inscribed as a World Heritage Site in 2017.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/taputapuatea.jpg" alt="Taputapuatea" width="320" height="161" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Michel-georges bernard · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Marae,_Raiatea_2.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
